CHEAP DISCRIMINATOR, in this order:
1. is the class @[mk_iff]? then the quantifier prefix is not yours;
2. does `iff_exists_appLE` / `iff_exists_appLE_locally` apply? then the Locally wrapper was never a real obligation;
3. is the residual conjunct swap a per-algebra mathlib iff? then the whole thing is (1) composed with (3).
If all three fire, what you have is a repackaging. It can still be WORTH landing -- the locus statement here is genuinely useful and did correct a wrong docstring -- but it must be published as locus, not as reduction. The tell that this needs checking: the file already contained a retraction of the identical shape.

